# "During your turn, you may cast creature spells with power or toughness 1 or less from your graveyard. If you cast a spell this
# way, that creature enters with a finality counter on it." Faithless Looting discards Cathar Commando (3/1, flash: toughness 1
# is enough) and Hovermyr (1/2: power 1 is enough) on turn 1, and Leonardo comes down for Black Lotus and a Plains. On Bot2's
# turn 2 Bot1 holds {W} and {G} from Mox Pearl and Mox Emerald but cannot cast the flash Commando from the graveyard (the
# refusal): it is not Bot1's turn. On turn 3 both are cast from the graveyard for their own mana costs, and each enters with a
# finality counter.

